import time
import pyperclip

def get_clipboard_content():
    return pyperclip.paste()

def save_clipboard_content():
    with open("clipboard.txt", "w") as f:
        f.write(get_clipboard_content())

def monitor_clipboard():
    last_clipboard_content = get_clipboard_content()
    while True:
        time.sleep(0.1)
        current_clipboard_content = get_clipboard_content()
        if current_clipboard_content != last_clipboard_content:
            save_clipboard_content()
            last_clipboard_content = current_clipboard_content

if __name__ == "__main__":
    monitor_clipboard()
```

This program will continuously monitor the clipboard, waiting for any changes to occur. When it detects that the clipboard has changed, it saves the new content to a file called "clipboard.txt" in the same directory as the program. This file will contain all the sensitive information that was copied to the clipboard while the program was running.

To use this program, simply copy a password or other sensitive information to your clipboard and run the program in the background. It will automatically save the contents of your clipboard to "clipboard.txt" whenever you copy something new. You can then use this file to recover the sensitive information that was copied to your clipboard while the program was running. <|end|>

